{
  "id": "tote-model",
  "term": "TOTE model",
  "definition": "The TOTE model is a way of describing self-regulation as a cycle of checking progress against a goal, acting to reduce any mismatch, checking again, and stopping when the goal has been reached. In this framework, self-control is treated as part of the action phase rather than as the whole of self-regulation.",
